instrument wingie
; wingie-proc-looper — line in caught and played like an instrument: a tape loop the top keys cut
; into stutters, a reel scrubbed from the bottom keys, a fader's movement recorded and looped,
; and a sampler that answers the line with its own slices. Line/Mic switch to line.
;
; every scene:
;   mode1            held: record (punch in, catch the reel, record the gesture, fill the sampler)
;   mode2            tap: the scene's second hand (a latch: see each scene)
;   keys1            where in the recording to play (each key a twelfth of it) or its speed
;   keys2            play it: each top key fires a slice, a stutter, a note
;   fader1 (Mix)     how much of the loop against the line
;   fader2 (Decay)   how long each piece is / how smooth the hand
;   fader3 (Volume)  the wear, the echo, the scene's colour
;   left LED         recording;  right LED  what plays back
; Step through the scenes with a held Mode button and a tap on the other.

the loop and the platter
------------------------
; hold mode1 and the line goes onto a four-second tape loop (over what's there; some of the old
; stays). The bottom keys play the loop at their pitch (C as recorded), octave1 at half or double
; speed. Every top key fires a stutter from one of the last beats of the loop (C the newest, B the
; oldest), pitched up the pattern; a tap on mode2 latches a steady stutter on the loop's own beat.
; fader1 the loop against the line, fader2 how long each stutter is, fader3 how worn the tape gets.
the loop is tapeloop seconds=4 gap=0.5
the hands are beatgrains 2 samplerate=half pattern=fifths burst=2
the beat is clock 4 rate=0.4
the latch is flipflop
the steady is vca
the oct1 is transpose
the mix is crossfade
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> loop
mode1 -> loop.punch
fader3 -> loop.age
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> loop.speed
loop.left -> hands
keys2.trig -> hands.clock
beat.eighth -> steady
mode2.tap -> latch
latch -> steady.gain
steady -> hands.clock
keys2.key -> hands.slices
fader2 -> hands.length
line.both -> mix.a
loop.left -> mix.b
fader1 -> mix.mix
mix hands.left -> guardl
mix hands.right loop.right -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
mode1 -> lights.left
hands.left -> lights.right

a hand on the reel
------------------
; hold mode1 to catch the reel (0.6 s of the line); let go and the bottom keys jump the head to
; each twelfth of it (C the start, B the end) while fader1 moves it by hand between them. Slow
; moves keep the pitch, fast ones rise like tape; fader2 how slowly the head follows the hand.
; The top keys pitch it through a shifter; the grains behind it sing it back and, with mode2
; tapped, feed back on themselves. fader3 how much comes back.
the reel is scrub 3 samplerate=half
the where is mixer
the shift is pitchshift
the oct2 is transpose
the back is graindelay 2 samplerate=quarter time=0.4 density=0.5
the latch is flipflop
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> reel
mode1 -> reel.record
keys1.key -80> where.in1
fader1 -20> where.in2
where -> reel.position
fader2 -> reel.smooth
reel -> shift
octave2 -> oct2
keys2.key -> oct2.pitch            ; C as it is, B almost an octave up
oct2 -> shift.pitch
shift -> back
fader3 -60> back.feedback
mode2.tap -> latch
latch -30> back.feedback
shift back.left -> guardl
shift back.right -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
mode1 -> lights.left
reel -> lights.right

the gesture
-----------
; hold mode1 and move fader1: the movement is recorded (up to 8 s) and loops when you let go; it
; reads the grains' tape (where in the last 0.3 s they play). Hold mode2 and move fader2: the
; same for the grain size. A bottom key pitches the grains; a top key held freezes the tape.
; fader3 how dense they are. Everything you played with your hands plays itself on.
the arm is gesture
the wrist is gesture
the g is grains 3 window=tukey spread=0.6
the oct1 is transpose
the shine is freqshift shift=0
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> g
fader1 -> arm
mode1 -> arm.record
fader2 -> wrist
mode2 -> wrist.record
arm -> g.position
wrist -> g.size
fader3 -> g.density
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> g.pitch
keys2.gate -> g.freeze
g.left -> shine
arm -2> shine.shift                ; the gesture also tilts a frequency shifter a little
g.left shine.up -> guardl
g.right shine.down -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
arm -> lights.left
wrist -> lights.right

the answering sampler
---------------------
; hold mode1 and the line is cut into 25 ms slices (the last 16 kept, each known by how bright
; and loud it is). Let go: every attack in the line is answered by the slice nearest its own
; brightness and loudness, chopped in time by a gate on those attacks. fader1 the brightness it
; looks for, fader2 the loudness; tap mode2 and it follows the line by itself instead. The top
; keys fire it too; fader3 how much spring it sounds in.
the sampler is concat
the ear is onset sensitivity=0.5
the latch is flipflop
the chop is slicer pattern=gallop len=0.6
the splash is spring
the wet is vca
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> sampler ear
mode1 -> sampler.record
fader1 -> sampler.bright
fader2 -> sampler.loud
mode2.tap -> latch
latch -> sampler.follow
ear.pulse keys2.trig -> sampler.trig chop.clock
sampler -> chop
chop -> splash
splash -> wet
fader3 -> wet.gain
chop wet -> guard -> out
line.both -40> out
mode1 -> lights.left
ear.env -> lights.right
